{%- comment -%}
  TIKVES LONDON · THE WINE PAGE BUY BOX · 7 Nov 2026 · into the pull request of 9 Nov 2026
  Built 7 Nov on the unpublished copy "TEST · buy box · 7 Nov (do not publish)"
  for his review, then carried into the Black Friday weekend pull request on
  9 Nov. Reference: the product pages of overtone.co and boombeauty.com, read
  7 Nov 2026, taken only as far as our rules allow.

  Rendered in parts from custom blocks in templates/product.wine.json, so each
  piece keeps its own place in the block order and can be moved in the editor:
    part: 'glance'    the at-a-glance strip under the price (tikves-pdp-copy)
    part: 'bf'        the Black Friday price, beside the button
    part: 'stock'     "Only N left." from the live count, at 60 or fewer
    part: 'delivery'  the free delivery sentence and the Christmas line
    part: 'cases'     "Also in these cases", one tap each
    part: 'find'      "Find your wine" by the button, like their quiz prompt
    part: 'faq'       FAQs under the body, word for word from /pages/faqs
    part: 'sticky'    the phone bar that shows once the button scrolls away,
                      and the phone first-screen spacing

  7 Nov 2026, afternoon: the same parts on cases, sets and spirits, from
  templates/product.json, so every product in the Black Friday offer
  (REF · BLACK FRIDAY 2026 v5, D4 and D17) carries the same buy box. The
  gift card is out of the offer and carries none of it.

  WORDS. Every line here is read from a live page, a metafield or a REF, and
  says where. The new ones were approved word for word on 7 Nov 2026:
  REF · WINE PAGE BUY BOX · NEW WORDING APPROVED · v1 · 7 Nov 2026.

  THE BLACK FRIDAY PRICE, part 'bf'.
  · Off unless the theme setting "Black Friday price on the shop"
    is on AND the depth setting holds a whole number from 1 to 99 AND the clock
    is inside Fri 27 Nov 00:00 to Thu 3 Dec 23:59 UK (moved from Mon 30 Nov
    on his word of 8 Nov 2026, "main event until Thursday 3"). D1 is 15%, his ruling
    of 7 Nov 2026 (REF · BLACK FRIDAY 2026 v7), and the depth setting defaults
    to 15. The switch is on by default since 10 Nov 2026, his word, with
    the Shopify discount scheduled for the same window. Turn it off if that
    discount is ever switched off.
  · PREVIEW ON A COPY ONLY. The 7 Nov test hook (a product.wine-bftestNN.json
    template) is gone, as the handoff of 7 Nov asked before any pull request.
    In its place: on a theme that is not the published one (theme.role is
    not 'main'), the block is rendered whatever the switch says, and the
    script decides by TL.now(), which snippets/tl-dates pins to ?tl_now= on
    such a theme. So ?tl_now=2026-11-28T10:00:00Z on a copy's preview address
    shows the weekend state on any date, with a Preview label and a dashed
    border, so no screenshot can pass for the live sale. On the published
    theme none of this exists: the switch, the depth and the real clock
    decide, and nothing on the address changes them.
  · The green price with the shop price crossed out, his word of 8 Nov 2026
    ("crossed out prices do like ezra suggested"), which replaced the green
    only ruling of 4 Nov 2026 and 6 Nov. The crossed-out figure is the live
    shop price, worked out here, never a compare-at price. While the block
    shows, the regular price block is hidden, so the shopper reads one
    price, what comes off, and what it was.
  · PRICE MATHS, as pull request 85: nothing here sets a price, the Shopify
    discount does. For a line of q bottles at price p and depth d per cent,
    off = round(p x q x d / 100) in pence, pay = p x q minus off. Shopify
    rounds per line. Every price on the shop is whole pounds, so at a whole
    number depth the figure is exact and no rounding can split it.
  · The basket shows the full price until the real discount exists. This
    block never creates or implies a discount on its own.

  ADDING: posts to /cart/add.js, then refreshes and opens the cart drawer with
  the same events as tl-mix-pdp (pull request 85) and tikves-gatc-handler. If
  the script fails, the form posts normally.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign tl_v = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign tl_p = tl_v.price

  comment
    Cases and sets are sold as one item, so their Black Friday line says
    "£X off", the words approved for the cases row. A bottle says
    "£X off this bottle". Read from the product type.
  endcomment
  assign tl_pack = false
  if product.type contains 'Case' or product.type contains 'Set'
    assign tl_pack = true
  endif

  assign tl_bf_on = false
  assign tl_d = 0
  if settings.tl_bf_depth != blank
    assign tl_d = settings.tl_bf_depth | plus: 0
  endif
  assign tl_d_int = tl_d | floor
  if tl_d_int != tl_d or tl_d < 1 or tl_d > 99
    assign tl_d = 0
  endif
  if tl_d > 0
    if theme.role != 'main'
      comment
        A copy, for preview: rendered whatever the switch says, and the
        script below decides by TL.now(), so ?tl_now= shows any date.
      endcomment
      assign tl_bf_on = true
    elsif settings.tl_bf_price
      comment
        The published theme. Server side, the window plus a day either side,
        because Shopify can serve a cached page. The script below is the
        final word on the minute.
        Fri 27 Nov 2026 00:00 UTC = 1795737600 · Thu 3 Dec 2026 23:59:59 UTC = 1796342399.
      endcomment
      assign tl_now = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
      if tl_now >= 1795651200 and tl_now <= 1796428799
        assign tl_bf_on = true
      endif
    endif
  endif
  if product.gift_card?
    assign tl_bf_on = false
  endif
-%}

{%- case part -%}

{%- when 'glance' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    AT A GLANCE. tikves-pdp-copy: dry or sweet, the grape, serving temperature
    and one food, near the price, each read from the same metafield the facts
    grid and the body use. Never an award, a price or a delivery line.
    Overtone runs the same strip ("At a glance") under its price.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign g_sw = product.metafields.wine.sweetness.value
    assign g_gr = product.metafields.wine.grape_blend.value
    assign g_st = product.metafields.wine.serving_temperature.value
    assign g_fd = product.metafields.custom.food_pairing.value | first
  -%}
  {%- if g_sw != blank or g_gr != blank or g_st != blank or g_fd != blank -%}
  <ul class="tl-bb-glance">
    {%- if g_sw != blank -%}<li>{{ g_sw }}</li>{%- endif -%}
    {%- if g_gr != blank -%}<li>{{ g_gr }}</li>{%- endif -%}
    {%- if g_st != blank -%}<li>Serve {{ g_st }}</li>{%- endif -%}
    {%- if g_fd != blank -%}<li>{{ g_fd }}</li>{%- endif -%}
  </ul>
  {%- endif -%}

{%- when 'bf' -%}
  {%- if tl_bf_on and product.available -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign bf_off = tl_p | times: tl_d | divided_by: 100.0 | round
    assign bf_pay = tl_p | minus: bf_off
  -%}
  <div class="tl-bb-bf" data-tl-bb-bf data-price="{{ tl_p }}" data-depth="{{ tl_d }}"{% if tl_pack %} data-pack{% endif %}>
    {%- comment -%} Approved 7 Nov 2026, REF · WINE PAGE BUY BOX v1. The green is #1f7a3a, kept on his word the same day. {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="tl-bb-bf__head">Black Friday · {{ tl_d }}% off</p>
    {%- comment -%} 8 Nov 2026, his word "crossed out prices do like ezra suggested": the shop price struck through beside the green price, inside the window only, worked out here from the live price. No compare-at price. The "£X off this bottle" line stays under it. {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="tl-bb-bf__price"><b data-tl-bb-pay>{{ bf_pay | money }}</b> <s class="tl-was" data-tl-bb-was><span class="visually-hidden">Was </span>{{ tl_p | money }}</s></p>
    <p class="tl-bb-bf__off" data-tl-bb-off>{{ bf_off | money }} off{% unless tl_pack %} this bottle{% endunless %}</p>
    <p class="tl-bb-bf__end">Ends Thursday 3 December at 23:59. <span data-tl-bb-left></span></p>
  </div>
  <style>
    html:not(.tl-bb-bf-off) .product-single__meta .product-block--price{display:none !important}
  </style>
  {%- endif -%}

{%- when 'stock' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    LIVE COUNT ONLY, REF · HORMOZI OFFER IN FULL v4 item L: "Only N left." at
    60 or fewer, the store's own number when the page is built. Same words and
    threshold as the product cards and the cart. Never typed, never faked.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if product.available and tl_v.inventory_management == 'shopify' and tl_v.inventory_quantity > 0 and tl_v.inventory_quantity <= 60 -%}
    <p class="tl-bb-stock">Only {{ tl_v.inventory_quantity }} left.</p>
  {%- endif -%}

{%- when 'delivery' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    DELIVERY, read 7 Nov 2026 in all four places tikves-delivery asks for:
    18 · CARRIER AND DELIVERY v6 section 4, the live shipping policy, the
    Delivery page and the delivery profile. All four agree: free at £100 or
    more to England, Scotland and Wales, never to the Isle of Man. The sentence
    is the shipping policy's own, word for word. No carrier, no service, no
    time. The Christmas line is 18 v6 section 5's, approved word for word for
    any surface, with its countdown from snippets/tl-dates.
    7 Nov 2026: shown only while the bottle can be bought. Under a SOLD OUT
    button, a delivery line and a Christmas order-by date read as a promise
    the page can't keep.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if product.available -%}
  <p class="tl-bb-delivery">Delivery is free on orders of £100 or more delivered to England, Scotland or Wales. <a href="/pages/delivery">Delivery costs and timings</a></p>
  {%- render 'tl-urgency', mode: 'line' -%}
  {%- endif -%}

{%- when 'cases' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    ALSO IN THESE CASES, kept from the page and from pull request 85, and
    moved up into the buy box. The cases are the hand-picked complementary
    products in Search and Discovery, the same list the old block read. Cases
    take the same Black Friday cut as the bottles (REF · BLACK FRIDAY 2026 v4,
    D17), so they show the green price when the bottle does. A case price is
    printed as set; nothing compares it to its bottles.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign tl_cases = product.metafields['shopify--discovery--product_recommendation'].complementary_products.value -%}
  {%- capture tl_cards -%}
    {%- for c in tl_cases -%}
      {%- unless c.available -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
      {%- assign cv = c.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}
      {%- assign c_off = cv.price | times: tl_d | divided_by: 100.0 | round -%}
      {%- assign c_pay = cv.price | minus: c_off -%}
      <div class="tl-bb-case">
        <a class="tl-bb-case__img" href="{{ c.url }}">
          {%- if c.featured_image -%}{{ c.featured_image | image_url: width: 200 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: c.featured_image.alt | default: c.title, widths: '100,200' }}{%- endif -%}
        </a>
        <div class="tl-bb-case__meta">
          <a class="tl-bb-case__name" href="{{ c.url }}">{{ c.title }}</a>
          {%- if tl_bf_on -%}
            <span class="tl-bb-case__price" data-bf-only><b class="tl-bb-green">{{ c_pay | money }}</b> <s class="tl-was"><span class="visually-hidden">Was </span>{{ cv.price | money }}</s></span>
            <span class="tl-bb-case__price" data-bf-alt>{{ cv.price | money }}</span>
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="tl-bb-case__price">{{ cv.price | money }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if cv.inventory_management == 'shopify' and cv.inventory_quantity > 0 and cv.inventory_quantity <= 60 -%}
            <span class="tl-bb-case__left">Only {{ cv.inventory_quantity }} left.</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <form class="tl-bb-form" action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}" method="post" data-tl-bb-add>
          <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ cv.id }}">
          <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
          <button type="submit" class="tl-bb-case__add">{{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}</button>
        </form>
      </div>
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- if tl_cards != blank -%}
  <div class="tl-bb-cases">
    <p class="tl-bb-cases__head">Also in these cases</p>
    {{ tl_cards }}
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}

{%- when 'find' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    FIND YOUR WINE, by the button. Overtone and BOOM both put a quiz prompt
    there, read 7 Nov 2026: "Not sure if this is right for you?" and a link
    to their quiz. Ours links to the Find your wine page, and the page's own
    title is the link. DRAFT for his yes: "Not sure this is the one?". Not on
    spirits or the gift card, which the finder doesn't cover.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- unless product.gift_card? or product.type == 'Spirit' -%}
    <p class="tl-bb-find">Not sure this is the one? <a href="/pages/find-your-wine">Find your wine</a></p>
  {%- endunless -%}

{%- when 'faq' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    FAQs ON THE PRODUCT PAGE, like Overtone's and BOOM's, read 7 Nov 2026.
    Every word is copied from the live FAQs page, /pages/faqs, read the same
    day: the heading, the intro line, five questions and their answers, and
    the closing line. Picked for what a shopper asks before buying. Nothing
    on carriers or delivery times, which stay off product pages. Change the
    FAQs page and this together.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- unless product.gift_card? -%}
  <div class="tl-bb-faq">
    <h2 class="tl-bb-faq__head">FAQs</h2>
    <p class="tl-bb-faq__intro">Quick answers to what we get asked most.</p>
    <details><summary><h3>Can I buy a single bottle, or mix my own?</h3></summary><div class="tl-bb-faq__a"><p>Both. There is no minimum order. Buy one bottle, one of our cases, or any mix of the two.</p></div></details>
    <details><summary><h3>Can I send it to someone else?</h3></summary><div class="tl-bb-faq__a"><p>Yes. Put their name and address in as the delivery address at checkout. Whoever takes it in must be 18 or over.</p></div></details>
    <details><summary><h3>How is it packed?</h3></summary><div class="tl-bb-faq__a"><p>In double-walled cases with dividers, because glass travels badly and we would rather it did not break at all.</p></div></details>
    <details><summary><h3>Do your prices include VAT?</h3></summary><div class="tl-bb-faq__a"><p>Yes. Every price on the site includes VAT, and so does the delivery charge.</p></div></details>
    <details><summary><h3>Do I need to be 18 to order?</h3></summary><div class="tl-bb-faq__a"><p>Yes. How we check, and what happens if we cannot confirm it, is on our <a href="/pages/age-verification">Responsible drinking and age verification page</a>.</p></div></details>
    <p class="tl-bb-faq__more">Not here? Ask the chat button, any time.</p>
  </div>
  {%- endunless -%}

{%- when 'sticky' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    THE PHONE BAR. tikves-storefront-audit allows a sticky add to cart only
    if it hides while the product form is in view. It shows once the main
    button has scrolled up out of sight, and hides again when it comes back.
    Phone only. One price: the green one while Black Friday shows, otherwise
    the shelf price. It adds the quantity chosen in the form.
    Also here, phone only: the first screen. On a phone the bottle photo
    filled the screen and the price and button sat a full scroll down; both
    references show title, price and the button by the first scroll. The
    main photo frame is held to 38% of the screen height on this template
    only, and the whole bottle fits inside it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if product.available -%}
  <div class="tl-bb-sticky" data-tl-bb-sticky hidden>
    <div class="tl-bb-sticky__info">
      <span class="tl-bb-sticky__name">{{ product.title }}</span>
      {%- if tl_bf_on -%}
        {%- assign s_off = tl_p | times: tl_d | divided_by: 100.0 | round -%}
        <span data-bf-only><b class="tl-bb-green">{{ tl_p | minus: s_off | money }}</b> <s class="tl-was"><span class="visually-hidden">Was </span>{{ tl_p | money }}</s></span>
        <span data-bf-alt>{{ tl_p | money }}</span>
      {%- else -%}
        <span>{{ tl_p | money }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    <form class="tl-bb-form" action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}" method="post" data-tl-bb-add data-tl-bb-sticky-form>
      <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ tl_v.id }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
      <button type="submit" class="tl-bb-sticky__add">{{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}</button>
    </form>
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}
  <style>
    .tl-bb-glance{list-style:none;margin:10px 0 0;padding:0;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px}
    .tl-bb-glance li{margin:0;padding:4px 10px;border:1px solid #B9AC9B;border-radius:999px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.4;color:#1F2328}
    .tl-bb-bf{margin:12px 0 4px;padding:12px 14px;border:1px solid #B9AC9B;border-radius:8px;background:#EAE3D9}
    .tl-bb-bf p{margin:0}
    .tl-bb-bf--preview{border:2px dashed #A64029}
    .tl-bb-bf__preview{display:inline-block;margin:0 0 8px !important;padding:2px 8px;background:#1F2328;color:#F5EFE7;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;border-radius:3px}
    .tl-bb-bf__head{font-weight:600;font-size:15px}
    .tl-bb-bf__price{margin-top:4px !important;font-size:15px}
    .tl-bb-bf__price b,.tl-bb-green{color:#1f7a3a;font-weight:700}
    .tl-bb-bf__price b{font-size:22px;margin-right:6px}
    .tl-was{color:#5c5a57;font-weight:400;text-decoration:line-through;text-decoration-thickness:1px}
    .tl-bb-bf__price .tl-was{font-size:16px}
    .tl-bb-bf__off{font-size:14px;margin-top:2px !important}
    .tl-bb-bf__end{margin-top:4px !important;font-size:13px}
    .tl-bb-stock{margin:8px 0 0;font-size:14px;font-weight:600}
    .tl-bb-delivery{margin:10px 0 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5}
    .tl-bb-delivery a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;white-space:nowrap}
    .tl-bb-cases{margin:18px 0 0}
    .tl-bb-cases__head{margin:0 0 8px;font-weight:600;font-size:15px}
    .tl-bb-case{display:grid;grid-template-columns:64px 1fr auto;gap:12px;align-items:center;padding:8px 0;border-top:1px solid #B9AC9B}
    .tl-bb-case:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid #B9AC9B}
    .tl-bb-case__img{display:block;background:#EAE3D9;border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden}
    .tl-bb-case__img img{display:block;width:64px;height:64px;object-fit:cover}
    .tl-bb-case__meta{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.35;min-width:0}
    .tl-bb-case__name{color:inherit;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600}
    .tl-bb-case__left{font-size:13px}
    .tl-bb-form{margin:0}
    .tl-bb-case__add{padding:9px 14px;border:1px solid #1F2328;border-radius:999px;background:transparent;color:#1F2328;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap}
    .tl-bb-case__add[disabled],.tl-bb-sticky__add[disabled]{opacity:.6;cursor:default}
    [data-bf-alt],html.tl-bb-bf-off [data-bf-only]{display:none !important}
    html.tl-bb-bf-off [data-bf-alt]{display:inline !important}
    .tl-bb-find{margin:12px 0 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5}
    .tl-bb-find a{color:inherit;font-weight:600;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}
    .tl-bb-faq{margin:28px 0 8px;text-align:left}
    .tl-bb-faq__head{margin:0 0 6px}
    .tl-bb-faq__intro{margin:0 0 12px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5}
    .tl-bb-faq details{border-bottom:1px solid #B9AC9B}
    .tl-bb-faq details:first-of-type{border-top:1px solid #B9AC9B}
    .tl-bb-faq summary{list-style:none;cursor:pointer;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;padding:14px 0}
    .tl-bb-faq summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
    .tl-bb-faq summary h3{margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.35;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0;text-transform:none}
    .tl-bb-faq summary::after{content:"";flex:0 0 14px;height:14px;background:linear-gradient(#1F2328,#1F2328) center/14px 1.5px no-repeat,linear-gradient(#1F2328,#1F2328) center/1.5px 14px no-repeat}
    .tl-bb-faq details[open] summary::after{background:linear-gradient(#1F2328,#1F2328) center/14px 1.5px no-repeat}
    .tl-bb-faq summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #A64029;outline-offset:4px}
    .tl-bb-faq__a{padding:0 0 14px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.55}
    .tl-bb-faq__a p{margin:0}
    .tl-bb-faq__a a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}
    .tl-bb-faq__more{margin:12px 0 0;font-size:14px}
    .tl-bb-sticky{display:none}
    @media (max-width: 768px){
      .tl-bb-sticky:not([hidden]){display:flex;position:fixed;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:20;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:10px 16px calc(10px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));background:#F5EFE7;border-top:1px solid #B9AC9B;box-shadow:0 -4px 14px rgba(31,35,40,.08)}
      .tl-bb-sticky__info{display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0;flex:1 1 auto;font-size:14px;line-height:1.3}
      .tl-bb-sticky__name{font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
      .tl-bb-sticky__add{padding:12px 18px;border:0;border-radius:999px;background:#A64029;color:#fff;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap}
      .product-section .product-image-main .image-wrap{padding-bottom:38vh !important}
      .product-section .product-image-main .image-wrap image-element{position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;display:block}
      .product-section .product-image-main .image-wrap img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain}
    }
  </style>
  <script>
  (function () {
    if (window.tlBuyBox) return;
    window.tlBuyBox = true;

    function money(c) { return '£' + (c / 100).toFixed(2); }
    function bottles(n) { return n === 1 ? 'this bottle' : n + ' bottles'; }
    function qtyInput() { return document.querySelector('.product-single__meta input[name="quantity"]'); }
    function qty() { var i = qtyInput(); var n = i ? parseInt(i.value, 10) : 1; return n > 0 ? n : 1; }

    // Black Friday block: the window, the countdown, and the figure for the quantity chosen.
    var bf = document.querySelector('[data-tl-bb-bf]');
    function bfUpdate() {
      if (!bf) return;
      var p = parseInt(bf.getAttribute('data-price'), 10), d = parseInt(bf.getAttribute('data-depth'), 10), q = qty();
      var line = p * q, off = Math.round(line * d / 100);
      var pay = bf.querySelector('[data-tl-bb-pay]'), o = bf.querySelector('[data-tl-bb-off]'), was = bf.querySelector('[data-tl-bb-was]');
      if (pay) pay.textContent = money(line - off);
      if (was) was.innerHTML = '<span class="visually-hidden">Was </span>' + money(line);
      if (o) o.textContent = money(off) + ' off' + (bf.hasAttribute('data-pack') ? '' : ' ' + bottles(q));
    }
    // The window and the minute come from snippets/tl-dates (TL.dates and
    // TL.now), so the end lives in one place; the same dates are the
    // fallback. TL.now is the real clock on the published theme. On a copy
    // it can be pinned with ?tl_now=, and the block then says so. The check
    // runs even with no block on the page (a sold out bottle), because the
    // cases row and the phone bar carry Black Friday prices of their own.
    var TD = (window.TL && window.TL.dates) || {};
    var start = TD.bfStart || Date.UTC(2026, 10, 27, 0, 0, 0), end = TD.bfEnd || Date.UTC(2026, 11, 3, 23, 59, 59);
    var now = (window.TL && window.TL.now) ? window.TL.now() : Date.now();
    if (now < start || now > end) {
      // Outside the real window: the block goes, the shelf price comes back.
      if (bf) { bf.remove(); bf = null; }
      document.documentElement.classList.add('tl-bb-bf-off');
    }
    if (bf) {
      if (window.TL && window.TL.pinned) {
        bf.classList.add('tl-bb-bf--preview');
        var tag = document.createElement('p');
        tag.className = 'tl-bb-bf__preview';
        tag.textContent = 'Preview · clock set to ' + new Date(now).toISOString().slice(0, 16).replace('T', ' ') + ' UTC';
        bf.insertBefore(tag, bf.firstChild);
      }
      // The buy box carries the depth, the end and the count here, so the
      // Black Friday line under the delivery sentence would say it twice.
      document.querySelectorAll('.product-single__meta [data-tl-lines] [data-tl-fill="bf"]').forEach(function (el) {
        var box = el.parentNode;
        box.removeChild(el);
        if (!box.querySelector('[data-tl-fill]')) box.parentNode.removeChild(box);
      });
      var left = bf.querySelector('[data-tl-bb-left]');
      if (left && window.TL && window.TL.left) {
        var l = window.TL.left(end, now);
        var pl = function (n, w) { return n + ' ' + w + (n === 1 ? '' : 's'); };
        if (l) left.textContent = l.kind === 'lastday' ? 'Last day, ' + pl(l.n, 'hour') + ' left.' : pl(l.n, l.kind === 'hours' ? 'hour' : 'day') + ' left.';
      }
      bfUpdate();
      document.addEventListener('input', function (e) { if (e.target === qtyInput()) bfUpdate(); });
      document.addEventListener('change', function (e) { if (e.target === qtyInput()) bfUpdate(); });
      document.addEventListener('click', function (e) { if (e.target.closest && e.target.closest('.js-qty__adjust')) setTimeout(bfUpdate, 0); });
    }

    // The phone bar: shown only while the main add to cart is out of view.
    // 7 Nov 2026: while it is up, the 10% badge, the access icon and the chat
    // button lift above it, so none of them sits on the bar's name or its
    // button. The lift rules live with the other stacking rules in
    // snippets/tikves-site-css.liquid (class tl-bar-up, height --tl-tray-h).
    var bar = document.querySelector('[data-tl-bb-sticky]');
    var mainBtn = document.querySelector('.product-single__meta form[action*="/cart/add"] [type="submit"], .product-single__meta button[name="add"]');
    function lift() {
      var root = document.documentElement;
      if (!bar || bar.hidden) { root.classList.remove('tl-bar-up'); return; }
      root.style.setProperty('--tl-tray-h', bar.offsetHeight + 'px');
      root.classList.add('tl-bar-up');
    }
    // Read on scroll, one frame at a time, rather than by intersection: a
    // jump that carries the button from below the screen to above it in one
    // go never crosses the screen, and an observer would not fire.
    function check() {
      var show = mainBtn.getBoundingClientRect().bottom < 0;
      if (bar.hidden === show) { bar.hidden = !show; }
      lift();
    }
    if (bar && mainBtn) {
      var ticking = false;
      var onMove = function () {
        if (ticking) return;
        ticking = true;
        requestAnimationFrame(function () { ticking = false; check(); });
      };
      window.addEventListener('scroll', onMove, { passive: true });
      window.addEventListener('resize', onMove);
      check();
    }

    // One add handler for the cases row and the bar. Same events as tl-mix-pdp.
    document.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
      var form = e.target.closest ? e.target.closest('[data-tl-bb-add]') : null;
      if (!form) return;
      e.preventDefault();
      if (form.hasAttribute('data-tl-bb-sticky-form')) {
        form.querySelector('input[name="quantity"]').value = qty();
      }
      var btn = form.querySelector('button');
      if (!btn || btn.disabled) return;
      var html = btn.innerHTML;
      btn.disabled = true;
      fetch('/cart/add.js', { method: 'POST', headers: { 'Accept': 'application/json' }, body: new FormData(form) })
        .then(function (r) { if (!r.ok) { throw new Error('add failed'); } return r.json(); })
        .then(function () { return fetch('/cart.js', { headers: { 'Accept': 'application/json' } }).then(function (r) { return r.json(); }); })
        .then(function (cart) {
          var num = document.querySelector('.cart-link__bubble-num');
          if (num) { num.textContent = cart.item_count; }
          var bub = document.querySelector('.cart-link__bubble');
          if (bub) { bub.classList.add('cart-link__bubble--visible'); }
          document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('cart:build'));
          document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('cart:updated', { detail: { cart: cart } }));
          document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('cart:open'));
          setTimeout(function () { btn.disabled = false; btn.innerHTML = html; }, 1500);
        })
        .catch(function () { btn.disabled = false; btn.innerHTML = html; form.submit(); });
    });
  })();
  </script>

{%- endcase -%}
